  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently RemoveAvatarEditorOnly and AssignAvatarNetworkIDs run at order -1024, while PreprocessCallbackBehaviours runs at -2048. There's not a lot of guidance for what the VRChat SDK intends to do at these orders, or what it might introduce in the future. As such, third-party extension authors are left to guess. Please document, at least in some broad strokes, where you expect third-party extensions to schedule their hooks.\n\nFor reference, here's what some popular editor extensions are using today:\n\n* VRCFury: -10000\n\n* Modular Avatar: -25 (with a hack to move the IEditorOnly removal later in processing)\n\n* Avatar Optimizer: 0\n\n* Virtual Lens integration with MA: -64 (which means I can't move the Modular Avatar hook without breaking this)\n\n* liltoon: 100",
